The fool took his lamps, but he did not take olive oil.
The wise ones took oil in vessels with their lamps.
The groom didn't come for a long time. So all the bridesmaids slept out of tiredness and fell asleep.
At midnight someone shouted, "This is the groom! Come and meet him!"
Then all the reelers woke up and prepared their reelers.
The fool said to the wise man, "Give us some of your oil, for our lamps are going out."
"'No,' they replied, 'there may not be enough for all of us. Instead, go to those who sell the oil. Buy some for yourselves.'"
So they went to buy the oil. But while they were on their way, the bridegroom arrived. And the bride's young women, who had been ready with him, entered into the wedding feast. Then she shut the door.
