The plan to kill Jesus.
Jesus finished saying all these things. Then he said to his disciples:
You know, after two days is the Passover. The Son of Man will be delivered to be crucified on the cross.
Then the chief priests and the elders of the people assembled. They met in the house of Caiaphas, the high priest.
They made plans to arrest Jesus cunningly. They wanted to kill him.
"But not during the feast," they said. "The people may become aroused." A woman pours perfume on Jesus.
Jesus was in the house of Bethany. He was in the house of a man named Simon, who had a skin disease.
A woman came to Jesus with an alabaster flask of very costly nard perfume. She poured it on his head as he sat at the table.
When the disciples saw this, they were indignant. And they asked, "Why this waste?"
The perfume could have been sold for a high price. The money could have been given to the poor.
Jesus knew this. He said to them, "Why do you trouble this woman? For she has done a beautiful thing to me."
You will always find the poor with you. But you will not always find me with you.
