Go to so-and-so's house in the town, and tell him, 'The teacher says, "My hour has come, and I will keep the Passover at your house with my disciples."'"
So the disciples did what Jesus had instructed them. They prepared the Passover meal.
When evening came, Jesus was sitting with the twelve disciples.
While he was eating, he said, "What I am going to tell you is true. One of you is going to betray me to my enemies."
The disciples were exceedingly sorrowful. And each of them began to say to Him, "It is not I, Lord, is it?"
Jesus answered, "He who dipped his hand in the dish with me, this one will betray me."
The son of man shall go as it is written of him, to go. But how evil it is for a Muslim, a son of man! It was more lovable to him that he had not been created.
