While Jesus was speaking to them, one of the twelve, who was called Judas, arrived with a large crowd armed with swords and clubs. They had been sent by the chief priests and the elders of the people.
Judas, who was to betray Jesus, had already agreed upon a signal with them, saying, "The one I shall kiss is the one; seize him."
Judas then went to Jesus immediately. And he said, "Peace be with you, Teacher!" And he kissed him.
Jesus answered, "My friend, do as you have come to do." Then the men stepped forward. They laid hold of Jesus and arrested him.
And behold, one of Jesus' companions drew his sword. And he struck the servant of the high priest, cutting off his ear.
