But all this was to fulfill the words of the prophets." Then all his disciples deserted him and fled. Jesus to the Council of the Sanhedrin
And those who had seized Jesus brought him to Caiaphas the high priest. And the scribes and the elders were assembled there.
Not too far away, Peter followed Jesus. He went into the courtyard of the chief priest. He entered and sat with the guards to see what would happen.
The chief priests and all the council were seeking what they might use against Jesus. They desired to put him to death.
But they found no evidence, although many false witnesses were brought in. Finally, two other witnesses came forward.
They said, "This man said, 'I am able to destroy the temple of God. And I am able to rebuild it in three days.' "
Then the chief priests took up their position, and asked Jesus, "Do you have no answer to make? What are these charges which these men are bringing against you?"
But Jesus remained silent. The high priest said to him, "I adjure you by the living God, tell us if you are the Christ, the Son of God."
"Yes, it is as you say," Jesus answered. "But this is what I tell you all. In the coming days, you will see the Son of Man seated at the right hand of the Mighty One. And you will see the Son of Man coming on the clouds of heaven."
Then the priest retreated from above him. He said, "He has said something very evil against God! Why do we need more witnesses than this? You have heard him say this evil."
"What do you think?" they answered: "He must die!"
Then they licked his face. One of them punched him with his fist. Others slapped him.
They said, "Jesus, speak to us about who struck you." Peter says, "I don't know Jesus."
Peter was sitting in the courtyard. A servant girl came to him. "I too was with Jesus of Galilee," she said.
But in front of them all, Peter said it wasn't so. "I don't know what you're talking about," he said.
Then he went out to the gate through which one enters into the paradise. And another woman saw him from another door. And she said to the people: "This one was with Jesus of Nazareth."
And again he said it was not so. And with an oath he said, "I do not know the man!"
Soon, those who had been standing near Peter drew close to him. "You must be one of them," they said. "Your speech betrays you."
Then he began to curse himself in wretched rags. He swore and said to them, "I do not know the man!" At that moment a cock crowed.
Then He mentioned about Jesus what He had said. 'The cock will deny Me three times before the rooster crows.' Peter went out, and wept bitterly.
